1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,170
This is a model of Berlin.

2
00:00:02,810 --> 00:00:09,070
Not the Berlin you know. This is the
city Hitler planned to finish by 1950.

3
00:00:09,670 --> 00:00:16,530
That dome would have held about 180,000
people, by its architect's own count.

4
00:00:16,930 --> 00:00:20,250
The model is real. The plans are real.

5
00:00:20,670 --> 00:00:23,750
And the plans for the rest
of the world survive too.

6
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:26,890
So when people ask what would
have happened if Germany

7
00:00:26,910 --> 00:00:31,070
had won the Second World War,
we don't have to imagine it.

8
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:32,390
They wrote it down.

9
00:00:32,710 --> 00:00:37,270
But first, the question underneath:
could they have won at all?

10
00:00:40,318 --> 00:00:44,710
Start with the money. Before the
war, the Allies' economies were more

11
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:47,990
than twice the size of
Germany's and its partners'.

12
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:51,710
By 1944, it was more than three to one.

13
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:55,310
The one close front was the
war against the Soviet Union.

14
00:00:55,330 --> 00:00:58,450
So a long war against Britain,

15
00:00:58,570 --> 00:01:02,410
America and the Soviets together
was close to unwinnable.

16
00:01:02,990 --> 00:01:06,090
If Germany could win
anything, it was a short war,

17
00:01:06,130 --> 00:01:09,050
in Europe, with Britain out of it early.

18
00:01:09,970 --> 00:01:14,370
And there was one moment when
Britain nearly got out. May 1940.

19
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:20,690
On the 9th of May, Neville Chamberlain
was about to resign as prime minister.

20
00:01:21,290 --> 00:01:24,430
The man he wanted to replace
him wasn't Winston Churchill.

21
00:01:24,450 --> 00:01:27,790
It was his foreign
secretary, Lord Halifax.

22
00:01:28,410 --> 00:01:30,450
The King wanted Halifax too.

23
00:01:30,970 --> 00:01:34,250
Halifax said no. He sat
in the House of Lords,

24
00:01:34,330 --> 00:01:37,070
and he didn't believe he
could lead a war from there.

25
00:01:37,470 --> 00:01:40,310
So the next day, the
job went to Churchill.

26
00:01:40,830 --> 00:01:45,590
Two weeks later, the British army was
trapped on the beaches at Dunkirk.

27
00:01:46,350 --> 00:01:50,050
And in the War Cabinet, Halifax argued
that Britain should at least find

28
00:01:50,070 --> 00:01:54,608
out what peace terms it could get,
with Mussolini as the go-between.

29
00:01:55,130 --> 00:01:56,630
For three days they argued.

30
00:01:56,790 --> 00:02:01,230
On the 28th of May, the rest of the
War Cabinet sided with Churchill.

31
00:02:02,110 --> 00:02:05,530
One minister who was there wrote
in his diary that when Churchill

32
00:02:05,550 --> 00:02:09,390
told the wider cabinet Britain
would fight on, they cheered.

33
00:02:10,030 --> 00:02:11,890
So here's our one change.

34
00:02:12,010 --> 00:02:15,070
On the 9th of May, Halifax says yes.

35
00:02:15,750 --> 00:02:17,910
We don't know that he'd have made peace.

36
00:02:17,930 --> 00:02:21,610
He wanted to explore terms, not surrender.

37
00:02:21,930 --> 00:02:27,590
But with him in charge, a deal in the
summer of 1940 becomes a real possibility.

38
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:30,230
That's the timeline we'll follow.

39
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:34,410
With Britain out, Germany
has no war in the west.

40
00:02:34,570 --> 00:02:37,650
No bombers overhead.
Nothing holding troops back.

41
00:02:38,770 --> 00:02:41,690
And Hitler had always meant to go east.

42
00:02:42,210 --> 00:02:46,610
In the real war, he invaded
the Soviet Union in June 1941.

43
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:50,650
In this one, he does it
with everything he has.

44
00:02:51,430 --> 00:02:53,250
America is the hardest part to call.

45
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:56,630
In the real war, its help
went first to Britain.

46
00:02:57,070 --> 00:03:00,470
With Britain out, it has far
less reason to fight in Europe,

47
00:03:00,490 --> 00:03:02,470
and nowhere to fight from.

48
00:03:02,930 --> 00:03:04,670
Does Germany win in the east?

49
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:07,550
Honestly, historians disagree.

50
00:03:08,110 --> 00:03:10,630
It was close even in the real war.

51
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:15,130
But that's the question this episode
asks, so in our timeline, it does.

52
00:03:15,510 --> 00:03:19,610
And from here, we don't have to
guess what Germany would do next.

53
00:03:19,670 --> 00:03:21,090
We can read it.

54
00:03:22,270 --> 00:03:26,750
Seven weeks before the real
invasion, on the 2nd of May 1941,

55
00:03:27,370 --> 00:03:31,670
senior German officials met to plan
how the army would be fed in the east.

56
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:36,370
Their minutes say that if Germany
took what it needed from the country,

57
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:40,430
"tens of millions" of people
would "undoubtedly" starve.

58
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:45,490
That wasn't a warning. It was the plan.

59
00:03:47,210 --> 00:03:49,610
Then there was the plan
for the land itself.

60
00:03:49,890 --> 00:03:52,890
They called it the
General Plan for the East.

61
00:03:53,450 --> 00:03:57,110
One version counted about 45
million people living there,

62
00:03:57,130 --> 00:03:59,770
and called for around 31 million

63
00:03:59,790 --> 00:04:04,730
of them to be removed, sent
east into Siberia over 30 years,

64
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:07,830
to make room for German settlers.

65
00:04:08,467 --> 00:04:10,770
In our timeline, nothing stops it.

66
00:04:10,950 --> 00:04:13,090
No Red Army comes back west.

67
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:18,170
By 1950, the plan is less than
ten years into its thirty.

68
00:04:18,190 --> 00:04:21,450
Everything it was written
to do is still ahead.

69
00:04:22,270 --> 00:04:27,570
In January 1942, at a villa
by a lake outside Berlin,

70
00:04:28,230 --> 00:04:32,010
senior officials met to coordinate
the murder of Europe's Jews.

71
00:04:32,710 --> 00:04:36,730
The record of that meeting has
a list, country by country.

72
00:04:36,750 --> 00:04:39,610
The total is over 11 million.

73
00:04:40,290 --> 00:04:43,310
The list includes countries
Germany never controlled.

74
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:48,406
England: 330,000. Ireland: 4,000.

75
00:04:49,110 --> 00:04:52,430
In the real war, about 6
million Jews were murdered.

76
00:04:53,090 --> 00:04:55,670
The killing stopped because Germany lost.

77
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:59,550
In our timeline, Germany doesn't lose.

78
00:05:00,070 --> 00:05:02,750
There is no liberation in 1945.

79
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:05,290
Britain had a list of its own.

80
00:05:05,310 --> 00:05:10,670
In 1940, the SS drew up a handbook
for the invasion of Britain.

81
00:05:11,470 --> 00:05:16,410
At the back are about 2,800
names of people to be arrested.

82
00:05:17,130 --> 00:05:18,490
Churchill is on it.

83
00:05:18,690 --> 00:05:22,810
In our timeline, a peace deal
means no invasion, and no arrests.

84
00:05:23,330 --> 00:05:25,630
But Britain now lives twenty miles across

85
00:05:25,650 --> 00:05:28,650
the water from a
continent run from Berlin.

86
00:05:29,390 --> 00:05:33,510
And its Jews are already
counted, on a list in Berlin.

87
00:05:34,210 --> 00:05:38,830
In August 1939, Albert Einstein
signed a letter to President

88
00:05:38,850 --> 00:05:43,130
Roosevelt warning that Germany
might build an atomic bomb.

89
00:05:43,690 --> 00:05:47,150
That fear is how America's
bomb project began.

90
00:05:48,170 --> 00:05:51,050
In our timeline, America
isn't at war in Europe.

91
00:05:51,630 --> 00:05:53,230
Does it still build the bomb?

92
00:05:54,030 --> 00:05:59,210
Honestly, we don't know. But the fear
that started it hasn't gone away.

93
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:02,930
If anything, in this world it's stronger.

94
00:06:05,310 --> 00:06:07,470
And at the centre of it all, Berlin.

95
00:06:08,230 --> 00:06:11,170
Rebuilt around one enormous avenue,

96
00:06:11,190 --> 00:06:15,770
with the great dome at one end and
a triumphal arch in the middle.

97
00:06:16,070 --> 00:06:18,470
Its new name was to be Germania.

98
00:06:18,610 --> 00:06:20,230
Due by 1950.

99
00:06:21,830 --> 00:06:28,137
In 1941, engineers poured a block of
concrete weighing about 12,500 tonnes

100
00:06:28,230 --> 00:06:33,630
into the Berlin soil, to test whether
the ground could carry that arch.

101
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:36,110
The limit was 6 centimetres.

102
00:06:36,130 --> 00:06:38,470
It sank about three times that.

103
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:44,130
So in our timeline, in 1950, a
triumphal arch more than a hundred

104
00:06:44,150 --> 00:06:48,610
metres tall goes up, on ground
that had already failed the test.

105
00:06:48,790 --> 00:06:53,510
The capital of a continent, built
on soil that couldn't hold it.

106
00:06:54,010 --> 00:06:58,570
Now look at what exists in our
1950, and might not in theirs.

107
00:06:59,150 --> 00:07:04,190
The United Nations, founded in 1945
by the countries that beat Germany.

108
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:09,270
The Berlin Airlift, when planes
flew food into a divided city.

109
00:07:09,710 --> 00:07:14,810
A democratic West Germany, with
a new constitution in 1949.

110
00:07:15,330 --> 00:07:18,530
Every one of them came
out of Germany's defeat.

111
00:07:19,170 --> 00:07:21,970
In our timeline, none
of them is guaranteed.

112
00:07:23,103 --> 00:07:24,950
And that's where the evidence stops.

113
00:07:25,850 --> 00:07:28,190
1950 was their own deadline.

114
00:07:28,830 --> 00:07:33,630
Past it, nobody knows, and anyone
who tells you otherwise is guessing.

115
00:07:34,470 --> 00:07:36,910
In the real world, the war turned.

116
00:07:37,450 --> 00:07:40,230
Work on Germania stopped in 1943.

117
00:07:40,970 --> 00:07:43,710
The dome was never built,
and neither was the arch.

118
00:07:44,170 --> 00:07:49,010
But the test block is still there,
on an ordinary street in Berlin.

119
00:07:50,170 --> 00:07:54,230
So that's what the world would have
looked like if Germany had won.

120
00:07:54,990 --> 00:07:58,630
Not our guess. Theirs.
The plans were real.

121
00:07:59,170 --> 00:08:01,250
The only thing missing was the victory.

122
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:04,270
This was UNHISTORY, from UNBUILT.

123
00:08:04,750 --> 00:08:08,850
Every picture in this video is real,
and the sources are in the description.

